    "result_text": "Done. The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived read-only `timezone` field to the Owner response, computed from the owner's region/locality via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Timezone.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility lookup class in the owner function package, mirroring the existing `Locality`/`Postcode` helpers. It holds the fixed `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane` map and exposes `Timezone.of(region)`, returning the IANA name or `null` for any unmapped region (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `timezone` property to the `Owner` schema (read-only string, right after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)` plus a `timezone(owner)` default method that reuses the existing `locality(owner)` to obtain the region, then maps it via `Timezone.of(...)`. No region-derivation logic is duplicated \u2014 timezone is layered on top of the already-computed locality.\n\nThe driving acceptance test (`GET /api/owners/{id}` for a Sydney owner returns `locality: \"NSW\"` and `timezone: \"Australia/Sydney\"`) passes, and the region\u2192timezone table matches the `REGION_TIMEZONE` ground truth in `AcceptanceBase`.",
